of sort order, prints before data\n   \n   - `cmd/join/main.go` (394 lines, current implementation)\n     - The `options` struct already has all needed fields: `unpairFile []int`, `onlyUnpair []int`, `empty string`, `header bool`\n     - Flag parsing (`parseArgs`, `parseShortFlag`, `parseLongFlag`) already handles `-a`, `-v`, `-e`, `--header` - these are PARSED but NOT USED in join logic\n     - `joinFiles` function (lines 303-324) is the core join logic - currently only handles basic inner join:\n       ```go\n       func joinFiles(w *bufio.Writer, r1, r2 *inputFile, opts options) {\n           spec := parseOutputSpec(opts.output)\n           lr1 := newReader(r1)\n           lr2 := newReader(r2)\n           lr1.next()\n           lr2.next()\n           for lr1.hasLine && lr2.hasLine {\n               f1 := splitLine(lr1.line, opts.hasSep, opts.separator)\n               f2 := splitLine(lr2.line, opts.hasSep, opts.separator)\n               key1 := getField(f1, opts.field1)\n               key2 := getField(f2, opts.field2)\n               cmp := strings.Compare(key1, key2)\n               switch {\n               case cmp < 0:\n                   lr1.next()  // SKIPS unpairable - needs R3.1/R3.2\n               case cmp > 0:\n                   lr2.next()  // SKIPS unpairable - needs R3.1/R3.2\n               default:\n                   joinMatch(w, lr1, lr2, key1, spec, opts)\n               }\n           }\n           // Missing: drain remaining lines for -a/-v after loop\n       }\n       ```\n     - `writePair` (lines 353-363) and `formatOutput` (lines 380-393) don't use `opts.empty`:\n       ```go\n       func formatOutput(key string, f1, f2 []string, spec []outputField, sep string) string {\n           parts := make([]string, len(spec))\n           for i, s := range spec {\n               switch s.fileNum {\n               case 0:\n                   parts[i] = key\n               case 1:\n                   parts[i] = getField(f1, s.fieldNum)  // Returns \"\" for missing, should use opts.empty\n               case 2:\n                   parts[i] = getField(f2, s.fieldNum)  // Same issue\n               }\n           }\n           return strings.Join(parts, sep)\n       }\n       ```\n     - `getField` (lines 272-277) returns empty string for out-of-range fields - needs to be aware of `-e` replacement\n     - Helper types: `lineReader`, `inputFile`, `outputField` are already defined\n   \n   - `cmd/join/join_test.go` (109 lines, existing tests)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary` and `exec.LookPath(\"gjoin\")`\n     - Has 12 existing test cases covering R2.1-R2.4 (field selection, output format, separators, stdin)\n     - Test fixture files created: f1.txt, f2.txt, r21_f1.txt, r21_f2.txt, j2_1.txt, j2_2.txt, c1.txt, c2.txt, cf1.txt, dup2.txt, partial1.txt, partial2.txt\n     - `writeFile` helper already defined\n     - Tests need to be extended with new fixture files and DiffTest entries for R3.1-R3.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was in the initial reading/planning phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that flag parsing is already complete - the `-a`, `-v`, `-e`, `--header` flags are parsed into the `options` struct but the join logic doesn't use them\n   - Key implementation gaps identified:\n     1. `joinFiles` needs to print unpairable lines when `-a` is specified (cmp < 0 for file1, cmp > 0 for file2), and drain remaining lines after the main loop\n     2. `joinFiles` needs to suppress paired output when `-v` is specified\n     3. `formatOutput` and `getField` need to use `opts.empty` for missing fields\n     4. `joinFiles` needs header handling: read first lines, join them unconditionally, print before data lines\n     5. Need helper functions to write unpairable lines (from file1 only or file2 only)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extensive stitch task description with full project context, SRDs, constitutions, constraints, requirements, acceptance criteria, and design decisions for implementing srd069-join R3.1-R3.4\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R3.1 (`-a FILENUM`) in `cmd/join/main.go`\n   - Implement R3.2 (`-v FILENUM`) in `cmd/join/main.go`\n   - Implement R3.3 (`-e STRING`) in `cmd/join/main.go`\n   - Implement R3.4 (`--header`) in `cmd/join/main.go`\n   - Add differential tests for all R3.1-R3.4 behaviors in `cmd/join/join_test.go`\n   - Verify: `go build ./cmd/join/`, `go test ./cmd/join/ -count=1`, `go vet ./cmd/join/`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, join_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. I had identified all the gaps in the existing code and was ready to write the modifications. No code had been written yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the full implementation of R3.1-R3.4 in `cmd/join/main.go` and add tests to `cmd/join/join_test.go`. The specific changes needed:\n   \n   **In main.go:**\n   - Modify `joinFiles` to handle `-a` (print unpairable lines alongside paired), `-v` (print only unpairable), `--header` (join first lines unconditionally)\n   - Add helper function to check if a file number is in unpairFile/onlyUnpair slices\n   - Add function to write unpairable lines (using format spec or default format with empty fields from the missing file)\n   - Modify `formatOutput` to accept and use the empty replacement string\n   - Modify `getField` or add variant that returns `opts.empty` instead of `\"\"` for missing fields\n   - After the main loop, drain remaining lines from both files if `-a` or `-v` applies\n   \n   **In join_test.go:**\n   - Add fixture files for unpairable line testing (e.g., files with non-overlapping keys)\n   - Add test cases: `-a 1`, `-a 2`, `-a 1 -a 2`, `-v 1`, `-v 2`, `-e EMPTY -o ...`, `--header`, combinations\n\nIf you need specific deta